    "body": "I think I understand this, but it'd be helpful to give an overview of the changes at a lower level, and why they work---both for me and for the future commit message.\r\n\r\nI think there are issues where you need to set memory[transferable] instead of dataHolder, but hopefully that's all. It's kinda pointer-related but not fatal. As discussed in IRC, I think your last comment isn't right; no copies are created in such a case.\r\n\r\nIn general I'd feel most comfortable signing off on this if you were able to walk through the algorithms the following cases, either mentally as a form of self-review, or in a comment here:\r\n\r\n- StructuredSerializeWithTransfer(null, « new ArrayBuffer(2) »)\r\n- StructuredSerializeWithTransfer({ x: { y: someArrayBuffer } }, someArrayBuffer), i.e. a case that requires recursion.",
